;; =============================================================================
;; Spec: Ariadne step 2f — runtime issuance for irreversible effects
;; =============================================================================

{:spec/title "Issue narrow runtime-owned grants for irreversible effects"

 :spec/description
 "Build the production issuance path that turns a runtime-approved canonical
  effect request into a short-lived ExecutionGrant. The basis is the active
  workflow-run identity plus an effect-specific preflight result: merge
  readiness for a PR, or deployment policy checks and provider dry-run for a
  deploy. The workflow runtime is the principal; agents may propose inputs but
  cannot mint or alter authority. Issuance occurs after the runtime preallocates
  the effect transaction ID and knows the exact target, but before the durable
  proposal and grant-aware decision are recorded.

  Workflow-start issuance is rejected because it creates a broad, long-lived
  authority object; phase-entry issuance is rejected because the exact effect
  target and preflight result may not yet be known.

  Issuance uses one explicit policy catalog keyed by effect class. Merge grants
  last 15 minutes and deploy grants last 30 minutes because deployment includes
  provider dry-run and rollback preparation. Both bind one preallocated effect
  transaction, carry :constraint/max-count 1, and set :grant/delegable? false.
  These are effect-policy decisions, not role defaults; absent constraint axes
  remain explicitly unbounded.

  Merge scope binds the effect transaction, workflow run, repository, and PR
  number. Deploy scope binds the effect transaction, workflow run, kustomize
  directory, Kubernetes context, namespace, and deployment name. A nil
  Kubernetes context is an explicit binding to the configured default context,
  not a wildcard. The issuer refuses incomplete scope rather than broadening
  it. It checks the revocation-for-cause eligibility predicate before calling
  execution-grant/issue.

  No inner agent receives a delegated merge or deploy grant in this slice.
  Agents propose work but never invoke these irreversible effects; the runtime
  retains authority and commits them. Delegating authority that a child does
  not exercise would enlarge the blast radius without enabling behavior."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :feature
  :scope ["components/execution-grant/**"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["Only deterministic runtime code may call the production issuer"
  "Issuance requires an effect-specific allow-class preflight result"
  "The grant principal is the workflow-run runtime identity"
  "The issuer must know the complete effect scope before minting a grant"
  "Merge policy is a 15-minute non-delegable one-transaction grant"
  "Deploy policy is a 30-minute non-delegable one-transaction grant"
  "Ceilings come from one effect-policy catalog, never an implicit role default"
  "Eligibility is checked before execution-grant/issue"
  "Callers cannot supply expiry, ceilings, or delegation state"
  "Issuer input and output are validated at the public component boundary"
  "Policy and grant fixture maps are constructed once and reused in tests"
  "Stratified design permits at most three layers per implementation namespace"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["The production issuer calls execution-grant/issue"
  "Issuance refuses an absent or deny-class preflight result"
  "A merge grant binds effect transaction, workflow run, repository, and PR number"
  "A deploy grant binds effect transaction, workflow run, kustomize directory, Kubernetes context, namespace, and deployment name"
  "Issuance refuses a request missing any required scope binding"
  "Merge grants expire 15 minutes after issuance"
  "Deploy grants expire 30 minutes after issuance"
  "Merge and deploy grants carry :constraint/max-count 1"
  "Merge and deploy grants carry :grant/delegable? false"
  "A principal with disqualifying breach history is refused issuance"
  "Malformed public issuer input returns a schema failure before persistence"
  "poly check reports 0 errors and 0 warnings"
  "full bb test is green"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :high
  :axes #{:correctness :policy-enforcement :governance-credibility}
  :theme :ariadne-grants
  :rationale "Without runtime-owned issuance, grant enforcement either remains bypassed or denies every irreversible effect."
  :blocks ["ariadne-merge-grant-enforcement.spec.edn"
           "ariadne-deploy-grant-enforcement.spec.edn"]
  :blocked-by []}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
